===========
Collections
===========

    >>> import nltk
    >>> from nltk.collections import *

Trie
----

Trie can be pickled, and loaded back through ``nltk.picklesec``, which only
rebuilds classes from the modules it is told to expect:

    >>> from functools import partial
    >>> from nltk import picklesec
    >>> roundtrip = partial(picklesec.roundtrip, allowed_modules=['nltk.collections'])
    >>> trie = nltk.collections.Trie(['a'])
    >>> roundtrip(trie)
    {'a': {True: None}}

LazyIteratorList
----------------

Fetching the length of a LazyIteratorList object does not throw a StopIteration exception:

    >>> lil = LazyIteratorList(i for i in range(1, 11))
    >>> lil[-1]
    10
    >>> len(lil)
    10
